title: Summer sea: notes from the last trip
status: published
date: 2026-10-09 19:00
labels: travel, photos
desc: A weekend by the sea in four paragraphs
comments: on
image: media/sea.jpg
---
We took the early bus, left our bags at the guesthouse and walked straight to the water.

The tide was out, the sand was cold, and the whole beach belonged to a few gulls and one very serious dog.

## What I would do again

- Take the first bus of the day
- Eat the noodles at the harbour stall
- Stay for the sunset, even if it is windy

## Packing list

1. Sunscreen, hat, towel
2. A book and sunglasses
3. Camera and a 50mm lens
4. A light jacket for the evening wind

Next time: the island ferry.
title: Winter Seoraksan: what to pack for a first winter hike
status: published
date: 2026-10-25 08:15
labels: travel
desc: A checklist for your first winter mountain
comments: on
image: media/seorak.jpg
---
Half of a first winter hike is the packing. Here is the list I wrote after Seoraksan last winter, exactly as it was.

## Don't leave without

- Crampons and gaiters
- Two pairs of waterproof gloves (one spare)
- Hot tea in a flask
- A head torch and spare batteries
- A power bank (phones drain fast in the cold)

## Dress in three layers

1. **Base layer** that dries fast
2. **Warm layer**: thin fleece or a light down jacket
3. **Shell** that stops wind and snow

> The sun sets earlier than you think in the mountains. Start down by three.

![A night full of stars](media/night.jpg)

The sky above the lodge after we came down. I would go back for this view alone.
title: A spring walk album: azaleas, canola and a dog
status: published
date: 2026-10-05 17:45
labels: photos, daily
desc: Four photos from this spring's walks
comments: on
image: media/azalea.jpg
---
Sorting spring photos in autumn is a little odd, but the colder it gets, the more I miss these colours. Here are this spring's walks in one place.

![Canola flowers under a blue sky](media/canola.jpg)
![A dog walking by the river](media/dog-walk.jpg)
![The cherry road](media/cherry.jpg)

## The routes

- **Azalea trail**: spring gate to the top and back, ninety minutes
- **Riverside canola fields**: thirty minutes by bike, best in the second week of April
- **The cherry road**: at dusk the pink is deepest

> Seasons never arrive all at once. They come one step, one flower at a time.
title: The cat who owns the window seat
status: published
date: 2026-10-27 15:20
labels: daily, photos
desc: A short story about a cat and a sunny window
comments: on
image: media/window-cat.jpg
---
Every afternoon at about three, the cat arrives, circles twice, and claims the window seat. I have stopped arguing.

## Three rules of the window seat

1. The sun belongs to the cat
2. Books may share the seat, but only if they are warm
3. Tea is allowed. Spilling is not

> Cats know exactly where the warmest spot is. So I follow the cat.

It is the calmest hour of my day.
